Human: What else can you tell me about Amazon Mechanical Turk?

Assistant: Amazon Mechanical Turk is an online marketplace and task management platform that sets up human intelligence tasks (HITs) to be performed remotely by "crowds"  (groups of people who are not employees) on a wide variety of topics.  Amazon Mechanical Turk was launched in 2005 as part of Amazon.com, Inc. 's Amazon.com. gut mechanical turk, an Amazon Mechanical Turk name for an individual who performs imaging categorization tasks online for wages.  HITs are made up of tasks in which participants use their own, often specialized knowledge to complete a particular assignment through the Amazon Mechanical Turk website.  The tasks are designed by Amazon Mechanical Turk clients, and may include data collection, transcription of audio or video recordings, image tagging, and further processing of data to create statistical models.  Data collected through Amazon Mechanical Turk is currently used for various kinds of digitization projects, including publication indexing, commercial web crawling, and psychological and thermodynamic experiments (e.g., estimating the ideal gas law).  While voluntary work, payment is provided by Amazon.com for task completion; workers are paid per task based on an individual "payment per assignment" price set by the worker or the client.
